 "meaning": "A short prayer of refuge to Kṛṣṇa as Viṣṇu, made almost entirely of names in the vocative: the bearer of conch, discus and mace, the one who lives in Dvārakā, Acyuta, Govinda, the lotus-eyed. The one request — rakṣa mām, ‘protect me’ — is grounded in the worshipper’s condition: śaraṇāgatam, ‘come for refuge’.",
